course: dictionary
lesson: 11870
title: One word, many meanings: born
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Born is one of them. Look at the words around it to find out which meaning is being used. «Mia was born in Ireland.» Here born tells you where her life started.
explain: «The baby was born at midnight.» Born means the baby came into life at that moment. When a sentence is about a baby, an animal or a birthday, born is about a start in time.
explain: «She is a born singer.» Here born does not mean coming into life. It means she has a natural gift for singing, something she seemed able to do from the start. Ask yourself: is the sentence about a start in time, or about a gift? The clues tell you which.
fact: Born means having come into life.
fact: Born can be a verb in «be born», as in «The lamb was born this morning.»
fact: Born can also describe a natural gift: «a born leader» is someone who leads easily.
fact: «Newborn» means a baby who has just been born, and «first-born» means the oldest child in a family.
fact: Mammals are born alive, but birds hatch from eggs. Both start life, but in different ways.
exercise: «The kittens were born in the barn.» What does born mean here? | Was a grown-up cat | Was lost | *Came into life | Lived in a barn for a long time
exercise: «She is a born artist; she draws beautifully without any lessons.» What does born mean here? | *Has a natural gift | Was taught in a school | Came from the city | Was drawn in pencil
exercise: «Ravi was born in Leeds, but his parents are from Pakistan.» Where did Ravi's life start? | Pakistan | Birmingham | *Leeds
test: Which word means a baby who has just been born? | Birthday | Borrowed | First-born | *Newborn
test: «He is a born leader.» What does born mean here? | Walked in front first | *Has a natural gift for leading | Was elected last year | Was chosen by a vote
exam: Which sentence uses born to mean a natural gift? | «Lena was born in Wales.» | *«Lena is a born goalkeeper.» | «Lena's baby brother was born in May.» | «Lena was born on a Monday.»
